WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:02.698
Hi, I'm Warble!

00:00:02.698 --> 00:00:06.652
Speech dot c p p is one small program that speaks, transcribes,

00:00:06.652 --> 00:00:08.300
and finds where someone talks.

00:00:09.808 --> 00:00:13.697
Each model is one file with its codec inside, behind one C

00:00:13.697 --> 00:00:16.614
interface, and speech flows from the very first frame.

00:00:19.342 --> 00:00:23.339
The command line, server and worker all call one C interface, which

00:00:23.339 --> 00:00:25.671
refuses options a model does not take.

00:00:26.091 --> 00:00:30.169
The request reaches a family port, which loads one file of weights and codec.

00:00:30.589 --> 00:00:34.507
It runs on ggml, on the CPU, Metal or Vulkan, and

00:00:34.507 --> 00:00:35.931
returns audio or text.

00:00:37.425 --> 00:00:41.670
The talker, a language model, reads the text and predicts each frame's first code.

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:45.528
A smaller code predictor adds fifteen more codes, one by one.

00:00:45.948 --> 00:00:50.487
A causal codec decoder turns sixteen codes into eighty milliseconds of audio,

00:00:50.487 --> 00:00:53.134
keeping its state so pieces join cleanly.

00:00:54.358 --> 00:00:56.158
The codec gets chunks of fixed size.

00:00:57.781 --> 00:01:00.486
The first frame goes alone, so sound starts early.

00:01:00.906 --> 00:01:02.578
Small chunks keep the player fed.

00:01:03.614 --> 00:01:05.972
Then four at a time, so stopping stays quick.

00:01:06.546 --> 00:01:10.653
Sizes never follow the clock, so a seed repeats its audio byte for byte.

00:01:11.842 --> 00:01:15.536
Streaming keeps up only if a frame is made faster than it plays.

00:01:15.536 --> 00:01:18.946
On our shared CPU each frame took about four times too long.

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:23.983
Drama 3 is mostly expert weights, which is why it asks for

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.587
thirty two gigabytes of memory.

00:01:28.433 --> 00:01:30.201
Streaming makes the first sound fast.

00:01:30.201 --> 00:01:33.149
Only a fast enough machine makes the rest keep up.

00:01:35.733 --> 00:01:39.948
One interface, one file per model, audio from the first frame, every

00:01:39.948 --> 00:01:41.704
stage checked against the original.

00:01:42.124 --> 00:01:44.209
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:44.209 --> 00:01:44.804
I'm Warble.

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:45.102
Bye!
